# json-schema-results.json, format-results.json and overlay-results.json
# are committed baselines that the respective runners compare against in
# CI with --check-baseline. The --optional variant of the JSON Schema
# suite is still gitignored: we don't track that baseline because the
# optional suite is a moving target we don't claim conformance against.
#
# format-results.json is the exception to that rule and is tracked, even
# though optional/format sits under the same optional/ tree. Two reasons.
# The corpus is pinned in corpora.json, so it stops being a moving
# target. And we do make a claim about format behavior: REPORT.md carries
# the headline number, and under the OpenAPI dialects format is an
# assertion, so a false reject there refuses real traffic.
json-schema-results-with-optional.json
openapi-results.json
